(over the heads of the wise men of the time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                     THE GOLD STANDARD IN AUSTRIA.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The adoption of the gold standard by Austria is now in progress, and) Tj T*
(there is every assurance that it will be carried into effect. That) Tj T*
(country had had the single silver standard since 1857, but was under) Tj T*
(a suspension of specie payments. When it was ascertained in 1879) Tj T*
(that the decline in silver was likely to be permanent the Government) Tj T*
(gave orders to the mints in both Austria and Hungary to receive no) Tj T*
(more of that metal from private individuals for coinage. The effect) Tj T*
(of this order was to make Government paper money the standard, and) Tj T*
(this paper varied from day to day in comparison with gold, as did our) Tj T*
(greenbacks before we resumed specie payments. Some silver was coined on) Tj T*
(Government account, but as a matter of fact that metal was discarded as) Tj T*
(a standard by the refusal to coin for private persons. Austria had a) Tj T*
(gold coinage, indeed, but the gold was commercial money only. It had no) Tj T*
(legal-tender faculty, but passed at its quoted value from day to day.) Tj T*
(Since 1879 the problem of finance in Austria has been two-fold, namely,) Tj T*
(to resume specie payments \(which must, under the circumstances, be) Tj T*
(gold payments\), and to fix a ratio at which all paper money and paper) Tj T*
(obligations should be redeemable. The ratio decided upon was that of) Tj T*
(119 paper to 100 gold, that being the average ratio prevailing in the) Tj T*
(market during the thirteen years from 1879 to 1892.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As the question of standard was really settled by Austria in 1879, when) Tj T*
(she closed her mints to silver, we are concerned to know how she came) Tj T*
(to take that step. The report of the special commission of the upper) Tj T*
(house on this subject, submitted last year, says that it had become) Tj T*
(clear as long ago as the decade 1860?1870, when Europe was becoming) Tj T*
(saturated with gold, that this was the only metal fitted to be the) Tj T*
(standard of nations of advanced civilization. ?Gold was dominant and) Tj T*
(the standard of value,? says this report, ?in all trade on a great) Tj T*
(scale as early as the fourteenth and fifteenth centuries, even though) Tj T*
(silver was then the standard in all domestic exchanges. * * * _In) Tj T*
(every age there is some metal dominant in the industry of the world) Tj T*
(which forces its way with elemental strength in the face of any public) Tj T*
(regulation, and in our day gold is that metal._?) Tj T*
ET
