(This is as good a statement as can be made of the reasons why not) Tj T*
(only Austria but all the other nations whose action we have examined,) Tj T*
(including the United States, have adopted the single gold standard.) Tj T*
(While Austria has been collecting her supply of the yellow metal we) Tj T*
(have heard a great deal about the ?scramble for gold.? Why is there a) Tj T*
(scramble for gold? Merely because gold is universally acceptable. All) Tj T*
(civilized people are willing to exchange their property for it to any) Tj T*
(extent, and this is the only thing they are willing to accept in that) Tj T*
(way without limit or reserve. That is a good and sufficient reason why) Tj T*
(there is a scramble for gold and why there is no similar scramble for) Tj T*
(silver.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                          A NATURAL EVOLUTION.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If we find a movement of civilized mankind going on steadily for a) Tj T*
(hundred years, working out in different countries uniform results which) Tj T*
(commend themselves to successive generations, the presumptions are all) Tj T*
(in favor of that movement being beneficial. At all events, the burden) Tj T*
(of proof is upon those who think differently. I am so well convinced of) Tj T*
(the benefits of the single gold standard that if all power were placed) Tj T*
(in my hands I would not introduce anything different from it. I should) Tj T*
(consider it presumptuous to attempt to interfere with an obviously) Tj T*
(natural evolution in human affairs. I should know, moreover, that such) Tj T*
(an attempt would be futile, because the first step to be taken would) Tj T*
(be to alter the preferences and likings of individual men. Society) Tj T*
(consists of aggregations of individuals, who in their private business) Tj T*
(prefer one ounce of gold to sixteen ounces of silver, or twenty-five) Tj T*
(ounces, as the case may be. Unless I can change this preference and) Tj T*
(liking I cannot alter the monetary standard of Christendom. It is this) Tj T*
(preference which paralyzes all the international monetary conferences.) Tj T*
(The secret thought of the delegates in the Brussels Conference was) Tj T*
(something like this: ?What would happen the day after international) Tj T*
(bimetallism if the commercial classes should continue to prefer one) Tj T*
(ounce of gold to sixteen ounces of silver?? Any responsible minister of) Tj T*
(finance must recoil before that query.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I think that the ?scramble for gold? would be worse the day after) Tj T*
(the bimetallic treaty than it was the day before, because everybody) Tj T*
(would suspect everybody else of gratifying his secret desire for) Tj T*
(gold at the expense of his neighbors. It should be remarked that) Tj T*
(the Brussels Conference, as a body, never touched the question of) Tj T*
(bimetallism, although some of the members improved the opportunity to) Tj T*
(make speeches on that subject. The Conference went to pieces on a minor) Tj T*
(question--that of buying a little more silver. The proposal was that) Tj T*
(the nations should purchase a certain amount of an article that none) Tj T*
(of them wanted. When the representatives of France and the Latin Union) Tj T*
(had the intrepidity to say that they would not recommend that policy) Tj T*
(to their governments, even if it should be adopted, the bottom dropped) Tj T*
(out of the Conference altogether. Although Mr. Bland has given his) Tj T*
(attention to this matter as a humorist, in a magazine article, I think) Tj T*
