(steps to give facilities for such knowledge. If it is a defect of our) Tj T*
(system that laws are passed ?unwittingly,? it is a defect which we) Tj T*
(share with all other governments, and it seems to us to be inherent in) Tj T*
(the representative system. At all events, we see no present cure for it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It thus appears that our correspondent, for whom, as we have said, we) Tj T*
(entertain much respect, has, in a single sentence, used three phrases,) Tj T*
(all of them important, and carrying with them the gist of the debate) Tj T*
(on a momentous question, without any clear idea of their meaning. He) Tj T*
(has used the word ?people? as though it were an entity separate and) Tj T*
(distinct from the only organ established for the expression of its) Tj T*
(will, but he has not told us where we can find this entity or how we) Tj T*
(can interrogate it. He affirms that the people have been deprived of) Tj T*
(a ?right? without telling us whether it is a legal or a moral right,) Tj T*
(or how it came to exist, or what portion of the civilized world regard) Tj T*
(it as a right, or how we are to know that it is a right, or anything) Tj T*
(about it. He has affirmed that the people were deprived of this) Tj T*
(right ?unwittingly,? implying that no law ought to be passed until) Tj T*
(all the people understand it. \(It is not necessary, according to the) Tj T*
(hypothesis, that they should approve it, but only that they should) Tj T*
(understand it.\) In using these phrases in this way he has ?begged) Tj T*
(the question? completely, but we presume that he was not aware that) Tj T*
(he was doing so. We have taken some pains to point out his unfounded) Tj T*
(assumptions because we know that he represents a good many people who,) Tj T*
(like himself, are honestly in error.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
